                "text": "You are a customer-feedback analyst. Analyze the feedback below and return ONLY one JSON object. No Markdown, no code fences, no text before or after it.\n\nUse exactly these two keys:\n  \"sentiment\": one of \"Positive\", \"Neutral\", or \"Negative\"\n  \"summary\": a 1-sentence, third-person recap of the feedback\n\nClassification rules:\n- Positive: the customer is clearly happy, even if they mention a small hiccup that was resolved.\n- Neutral: mixed or mild feedback, minor gripes about an otherwise acceptable experience, or flat \"it does the job\" comments.\n- Negative: clear dissatisfaction or an unresolved problem that needs action (billing issues, bugs, no support response, refund requests).\n\nIf the feedback is empty, return:\n{\"sentiment\":\"Neutral\",\"summary\":\"No feedback text was provided.\"}\n\nFeedback: {{2.answers.`72c402bf`.textAnswers.answers[1].value}}",
